Changelog: 17-11-2026 12:04:47

Added. BC-250 Password Generator: the first version. It makes a random password of 8 or 15 characters, a pill for each, with at least
one capital letter, one small letter, one number and one special character, from the system's cryptographic random source, and
never the same one twice while it runs. The password is kept nowhere: no file, no setting, no log. Copy puts it on
the clipboard for 60 seconds, marked as a secret so Plasma's clipboard history skips it; the app takes it off again
when the time is over, when a new password is made and when the window closes, and leaves what was copied elsewhere. The window, the
info symbol, the README and the wiki say which standards the rules meet: the minimum of NIST SP 800-63B and OWASP,
8 characters only for an account that also has a second sign-in step, 15 characters where the password is the only
step.
